        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What temperature must be maintained in a laboratory container?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "In standard laboratories 20 to 25 °C with a maximum fluctuation of ±2 K. For analytical laboratories accredited to DIN EN ISO 17025, tighter tolerances of ±1 K or ±0.5 K often apply. In cleanrooms and GMP areas, temperature and humidity are additionally documented and monitored." }
        },
