          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does a laboratory container need negative-pressure control?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Not always, but in many cases yes. For work with hazardous substances, biological agents (BSL-2/3) or odorous substances, negative pressure is prescribed in order to prevent the spread of contaminated air. Typical differential pressure is −10 to −30 Pa relative to adjacent areas." }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How high is the energy consumption of HVAC in a laboratory container?",
